Australian Product Guide — National-category expansion current release record
Release date: 2026-08-17
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: institutional v9 consumer design and navigation, v11 footer, national-category discovery layer, Decision Lab / explainable recommendation journeys, My APG local-first workspace with optional account sync, universal search, comparison, category/product/guide/trust surfaces, responsive accessibility hardening, privacy-first analytics consent and Amazon Associates controls. Architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement.

Catalogue truth: 387 maintained products; 74 populated categories; 145 represented brands. The maintained set includes 30 newly researched manufacturer-verified products across televisions, laptops, washing machines, fridges, dishwashers and smartphones. These new records use exact Australian manufacturer sources and explicitly state that APG has not performed hands-on testing. Existing starter-evidence records remain labelled and are not represented as equivalent to deeper research.

National evidence truth: the six newly introduced high-intent categories each contain five current Australian models with manufacturer-backed identity, maintained decision factors, trade-offs, FAQs, comparison pathways and Decision Lab/search coverage. Live price is not asserted where APG does not maintain a current price feed.

Amazon Australia retailer truth: 22 verified exact product destinations remain in the verified direct-link register. Other maintained products use transparent model-specific search/further-verification fallbacks rather than guessed ASINs. Eligible affiliate destinations use tag auproductguid-22. Retailer/affiliate availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Multi-retailer truth: APG is architected for broader exact Australian retailer coverage, but it does not claim whole-of-market price comparison. JB Hi-Fi, The Good Guys, Officeworks, Appliances Online and other relevant retailer paths remain PLANNED until exact-model, data-rights and commercial requirements are verified. No new affiliate programme or commercial agreement is activated by this release.

Imagery truth: exact external product photography is not claimed unless rights and model identity are verified. APG-authored semantic/category visuals remain the controlled fallback where authorised exact photography is unavailable. The national experience corrects legacy headphone fallback visuals for the six new category families with neutral semantic identifiers rather than fabricated product imagery.

Privacy/analytics: Google Analytics remains opt-in. Analytics storage defaults to denied and the GA script is loaded only after the visitor allows analytics. Essential browser storage remains available for privacy preferences and core/local-first research functionality. Account creation is optional and does not affect recommendations.

Current release changes: adds six nationally important categories and 30 manufacturer-verified product records; opens search to those categories; removes stale unsupported-category messaging; adds a national buying-decisions homepage layer; separates manufacturer evidence from retailer commerce more clearly; corrects retailer-hub exact-link counting; adds distinct national-category decision starting points; corrects evidence freshness labelling; preserves the existing accessibility, mobile assistant, privacy, security, SSR and performance architecture.

Release discipline: GitHub main is authoritative; Vercel Production must match the current source SHA; public canonical pages, new category/product routes, search, retailer/trust surfaces, SEO/structured data and responsive behaviour must be verified before the release is treated as complete. Historical 257-product / 48-category and 357-product / 68-category release snapshots are SUPERSEDED by this record once the matching Production deployment is verified.
